00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:52.500
Kamogawa Spirit

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:56.920
Wait, Izo.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:58.710
I said wait!

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:02.630
I can’t wait. Array’s Ovid is not responding.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:05.850
Which means one of us has to go down there and rescue him.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:10.430
The enemy Ovid signal wasn’t like anything we’ve ever seen.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:13.020
Are you saying that they brought out the Vox?

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.610
We can’t overrule that.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:18.400
If they already have the Vox,

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.610
it’s possible “Memoria” has been achieved as well.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.900
So they’ve found a pilot.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.120
All the more the reason for me to head out.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.120
I’m the best Ovid pilot in De Metrio.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.000
Izo!

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.960
Using the power of the Vox to crush Le Garite is our destiny!

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:40.460
No time like now to gauge the power of the legendary weapon that will eventually become ours.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:49.720
<i>If I don’t come back, get out and save yourself.</i>

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:02.780
I was tricked. I was totally tricked!

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:05.570
No one told me that there was going to be a second time!

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:11.290
Did she pretend to be my comrade just to lull me into piloting that Ox thingy?

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:14.040
Were those memories false too, then?

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:25.800
No, that was real… I think.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.680
Or were they?

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:34.390
Which is it? I’m so confused!

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.280
Yikes! They’re all from Youko!

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.900
I wonder what’s up?

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:49.950
NO SERVICE {sign}

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:49.950
No service.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.490
Yes, one bar!

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.250
It’s gone.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.420
Oh wait!

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:10.760
Hey…

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:16.850
Does this mean that your cousin beat that thing?

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:31.320
Seeing how it’s not moving, I guess it does.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.950
What does this mean?

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.490
Did your cousin actually manage to pilot that thing?

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:39.080
I thought she could only ride a bicycle.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.040
Maybe she actually got a scooter license.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.460
That’s not enough to pilot a robot!

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.670
It must be the people here.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:48.630
They’re hiding something!

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:53.510
We’ve spent five years trying to figure out the OOPArts with no success.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:57.640
Yet the guys here built a robot out of it in six months!

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.230
There’s got to be some secret to—!

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.110
U-Um…

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:04.900
Shh!

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.660
You stay here.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:14.080
Wait, please don’t leave me alone here!

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:20.330
What were you planning to do if Kyouno Madoka failed to activate Vox Aura?

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:25.500
Those who’ve achieved Memoria with the Vox become its one and only pilot.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:30.680
Even if Vox Aura falls into enemy hands, as long as we safeguard Miss Kyouno Madoka,

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.050
we have an even chance of winning.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:34.510
The same can be said should their positions be reversed.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:41.230
We could have accelerated her organic response with the Vox,

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:45.060
but it was risky, so I wanted to avoid doing so if at all possible.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:46.690
In any case,

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:50.320
we didn’t really have a viable countermeasure in the first place.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:52.910
I’m glad that thing actually moved.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.910
I also learned quite a bit thanks to that.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:08:01.830
You don’t give a damn about protecting this planet, inside that head of yours.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:05.750
Protecting the Vox equates to protecting Earth.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:10.300
Whose idea was it to make the Vox battle in the forefront?

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:13.630
Weapons from Earth are useless against them.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:18.600
Then why don’t you take the Vox and get off this planet?

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:22.980
Then Earth would fall under their sphere of control.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:24.100
Such a future would be bleak.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:25.980
Fine.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.980
So what now, then?

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:31.490
Will that kind of gamble work twice against them?

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:35.870
Judging solely from the performance of the craft, its power surpasses that of the enemy’s.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:39.080
The rest depends on her.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.410
So we’ll just have to see where the wind takes us?

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:44.170
You could say that.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.420
Can I ask you one last question?

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.630
Ask me anything.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:52.260
Is the main force really coming?

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:56.340
Immediately. Right after the war on their side is over.

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:02.390
Cap.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:03.390
What is it?

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.640
The pilot has run away.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:14.610
Oh no. I’m completely lost.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.530
Ouch!

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:20.160
Oww…

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.290
Come on!

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.670
It looks similar…

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.630
I guess it’s a little different.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.550
Who’s there?

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:33.840
Please wait!

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:37.090
Wait!

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:43.520
Excuse me! I’m…

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:46.020
Lost!

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.770
You too?!

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.770
You too?! {overlap}

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:54.740
Excuse me, but who are you?

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:58.200
The pilot… or… rather…

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.740
I’m Kyouno Madoka. And you?

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:02.990
I’m Muginami.

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:05.120
Say, Miss Muginami…

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:06.580
Roger that!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:09.500
Then, I’m going to look over there.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.000
You go that way.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.550
Oh, okay.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:15.090
Wait now…

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.050
So what do I do?

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:20.930
Found you.

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:28.690
I told you, I wasn’t trying to run away.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:31.150
It’s all right. I understand how you feel.

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:33.480
You do?

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:39.780
To be honest, I wish I could help more, instead of forcing everything onto you.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:43.660
But I could only fly it.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.080
Uh… What are you talking about?

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:51.080
I’m sorry, I…

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:08.140
There’s no way I’m going to fit into this.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:12.190
Help me out.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:19.400
<i>Can you do it?</i>

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:22.990
Not sure. Let’s see where the wind takes me.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:24.740
<i>Good answer.</i>

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:27.040
<i>Now listen calmly.</i>

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:29.000
<i>An enemy has appeared.</i>

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.540
<i>Presently, its location is 100 klicks southeast of Oshima.</i>

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:34.500
<i>It’s heading this way at mach 2.</i>

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.380
<i>Looks like it’ll engage us in three minutes.</i>

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.550
Th-Three minutes?!

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:42.090
<i>We will control the craft during Piercer Mode.</i>

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:45.640
<i>All you have to do is sit tight, just like last time.</i>

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.180
I have a question.

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:49.430
Was that last crash an accident?

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.230
Crash?

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:53.600
I believe she’s referring to what triggered the Form Change.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:54.440
Oh…

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:57.020
<i>It wasn’t an accident. It was planned.</i>

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:59.780
So we’re going to do that again?

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.400
<i>Correct.</i>

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.530
Okay, I understand.

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:06.660
<i>Kyouno.</i>

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.450
Yes?

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.450
<i>The future of our planet rests in your hands.</i>

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:11.080
Huh?!

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:12.460
<i>We’re counting on you.</i>

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.580
What?! Wait a minute!

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.920
I can’t handle that kind of pressure right now!

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:20.420
The whole planet? I’ve never even been to Tokyo!

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:22.880
Commencing Vox Aura A.I. Remote System check.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.760
Codes 1 through 11 are clear.

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:29.060
Pilot’s heart rate, blood pressure, respiratory rate… all normal.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.560
Opening barrier wall number two.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:34.100
Enemy unit two is approaching quickly.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:34.810
Vox Aura will engage the enemy… in approximately 100 seconds. {overlap}

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.810
A.I. Remote Systems are normal.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.690
No effect on the Vox System.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.780
Shuttle locks are open. {overlap}

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:42.860
Check complete. All systems go.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:48.030
I’m starting to get really nervous.

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:52.910
The Vox System is silent like the last time.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:56.830
Let’s hope she pulls through.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.880
Vox Aura, launching!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:32.410
An Ovid signal…

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:35.160
It’s not Array’s, so that means…

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:36.620
The Vox!

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:41.550
<i>You should see the enemy straight ahead.</i>

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.800
I see it… a black one.

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:45.130
<i>We’re going in head on!</i>

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:45.880
What?!

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:50.300
The hell with it… charge!

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:51.970
So you want to fight?

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.560
Bring it on!

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.330
What happened?!

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:14.500
We don’t know, sir!

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:19.040
The Vox System suddenly started up and is overriding the A.I. Remote!

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.830
What’s going on?!

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:23.500
Are you telling me she can control it in Piercer Mode as well?!

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:27.840
It appears the girl really is a perfect match for Vox Aura, isn’t she?

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:29.680
You should be concerned, too.

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.180
All stations, prepare for attack!

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:39.020
This isn’t it either! This place is too big!

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.150
Let’s go back inside.

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:42.940
That’s…

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:47.820
What’s it doing?

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.200
It’s running away?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:02.210
What’s going on?!

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.760
If you’re the real deal, then let’s see how you’ll handle this!

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:12.850
Vox Aura’s power grid is failing.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:14.050
This is bad…

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:23.310
What is the status of the pilot?

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:24.770
Her vital signs are normal.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.480
The craft, however, has shut down completely!

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.040
Where are you going?

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:47.500
Can you handle it, my lady?

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:00.850
You fear the legend.

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:04.770
Can you really accept the Vox in your current state?

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:13.860
This is what Array lost to?

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:43.690
It’s no use! I can’t see a thing!

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:03.500
Who am I kidding?

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:05.920
It was a crazy idea to begin with.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.170
Me, a pilot…

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:21.430
Incoming Call{sign}

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:21.430
Youko Nakaizumi{sign}

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:21.430
Youko…

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:23.770
Hello?

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.440
<i>Where are you now?</i>

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.400
Inside a robot…

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.650
I see…

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:33.280
Patching her through.

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:35.280
<i>Wait… You’re not surprised?</i>

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.160
Cell phones work in there?!

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.030
Where’s that call coming from?

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:39.200
Within Pharos premises, sir.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:44.330
<i>Why are you piloting a robot?</i>

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:47.710
Well, one thing led to another, and…

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:51.750
Oh, yeah. I wanted to ask you…

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:55.800
Did something happen to me when I almost drowned ten years ago?

00:17:57.550 --> 00:17:59.550
Do you even remember it?

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:03.810
Yeah, I remember it very well.

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:08.270
It seems like I met this robot back then.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.560
Where is the enemy unit?

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.360
Distance from Vox Aura: 200.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.400
It’s inside that black smoke.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:14.740
Who is that?

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:17.950
Damn… of all the places.

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:20.820
She’s a marine archeologist.

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:25.750
She’s been snooping around ever since our foundation confiscated her research regarding Vox Aura.

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:28.040
Then she’s…

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:29.830
The pilot’s cousin.

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:33.250
The one opposed to Kyouno Madoka piloting Vox Aura.

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:38.260
This robot is amazing.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.430
It moves exactly the way I want it to.

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:44.140
I was scared at first, but I got the hang of it quickly.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.600
It was quite fun, to be honest.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:49.100
<i>Meaning it’s not anymore?</i>

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:52.730
m<i>Well, after giving it some thought…</i>

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:56.690
Enemy unit two, distance from Vox Aura: 130!

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:01.070
<i>It seems a lot of people are</i>

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.780
<i>relying on me to pilot this robot.</i>

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:09.920
I want to live up to their expectations as best I can.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:13.340
I don’t want to disappoint anyone, but…

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:21.010
When I started thinking about that, it stopped moving.

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:24.350
You’ve got some nerve!

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:27.850
<i>Just who the hell do you think you are?!</i>

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:32.020
That thing’s not moving because you’re acting like you’re doing a favor!

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:35.520
Not that you have to feel grateful to them for letting you pilot that thing.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:37.990
But if you decided to do it,

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:40.610
then stand by the decision you made!

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:42.490
If that bothers you, then you should…

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:45.330
quit the Jersey Club!

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.960
<i>You’re so irritating!</i>

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:59.130
Yeah, you’re right. You are absolutely right, but…

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:03.840
It pisses me off hearing that coming from you, Youko!

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:06.510
It drives me nuts!{SHE HATES IT!}

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:15.110
Distance from enemy unit: 20.

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:30.870
Distance: ten, nine!

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:32.540
What are you doing? Move!

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:33.710
Eight! Seven! {overlap}

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:36.540
Six! Five! Four!

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.050
Vox System online!

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:41.130
Distance to enemy unit?

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:42.050
Zero…!

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:04.740
All right!

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:07.160
What? What happened?!

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:10.790
An unknown craft has broken through the atmosphere!

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:11.750
Where is it heading?

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:13.330
Right here!

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:17.170
What?

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:30.470
A pincer attack?

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:32.970
Kirius, what are you—?

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:37.810
I can’t sit back and watch this anymore.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:40.480
If we’re going to die, we’ll die together!

